ASCII Quests (apps/ascii)

The games (games/*.js)
  Caverns of Kroz II, Dungeons of Kroz II, Kingdom of Kroz II, Return to
  Kroz, Temple of Kroz, The Final Crusade of Kroz and The Lost Adventures of
  Kroz, by Scott Miller; published by Apogee Software (1987-1990).
  Copyright (C) 1987, 2009 Apogee Software, Ltd. In March 2009 Apogee
  released their source code under the GNU General Public License, version
  2 or later (COPYING here; GNU.TXT in the source archive).
  The source comes from Apogee's krozfree.zip, as imported unchanged into
  https://github.com/tangentforks/kroz (commit
  5d080fb4f2440f704e57a5bc5e73ba080c1a1d8d), folder source/ only. The
  games' Pascal files are unchanged; frunk.store's translator
  (tools/kroz/pascal.mjs) turns each game into JavaScript. The complete
  source for the files in games/, with the translator and the build
  script, is kroz-src.tar.gz next to this file. The compiled games in the
  same zip are freeware with all rights reserved and aren't used.
  "Kroz" is a registered trademark of Apogee Software, Ltd. ASCII Quests
  and frunk.store aren't affiliated with or endorsed by Apogee Software or
  3D Realms.

The runtime (runtime.js, worker.js, speaker.js, ascii.js)
  frunk.store's own: a text screen, keyboard, PC speaker and files that
  behave like Turbo Pascal's Crt unit on a PC, for the translated games.
  Released under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later, like
  the games.

The font (font.js)
  The Linux kernel's 8x16 VGA console font, lib/fonts/font_8x16.c at tag
  v6.12 (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git),
  GPL-2.0. Converted to base64 by tools/build-kroz.mjs.
